c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"de8c15d2ec22e047bdea298e3007340c21b033e37b4ac50bd670b978dc0fdd5d","event_uuid":"a10cff3a-16c2-46d2-9f9c-a841f65ec51a","position":{"commit_sha":"0bf8a7efebd41486bd019f3c0f445864c4d07fe8","position":"1787898672062884629-a10cff3a-16c2-46d2-9f9c-a841f65ec51a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"d137d3d0220409ab4a321e2acb843ad5ceaa3227c871146d15b7aab6000e4322","event_uuid":"9936e5d1-c3b7-423e-99eb-5d6cbc1310bc","position":{"commit_sha":"0cb0d0b3a72ded24b08f726cf53b10997f956f56","position":"1787899599142983409-9936e5d1-c3b7-423e-99eb-5d6cbc1310bc"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-247_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"41c69740-e628-4506-a328-65f32258a98e","comments":[],"created_at":1787898197372353231,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"c83f95c1-4829-442d-812d-52849fd80c95","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b928-3ab6-5985-417b"},{"link_uuid":"9936e5d1-c3b7-423e-99eb-5d6cbc1310bc","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"cde0-da07-78a4-4c23"}],"description":"## Summary\n\nTwo defects in one place, found while mitigating the tickets-branch write storm.\n\n**1. The documented rollback names a table that is never parsed.** `rebar.toml:38` tells operators\nto scope the enrichment drain with:\n\n    [tool.rebar.llm] overlap_drain = \"off\"\n\nThat table does not exist in this config's schema. The real table is `[llm]` (`rebar.toml:198`).\nAn operator who follows the instruction gets **no error and no effect** — the key is silently\nignored and the drain keeps running at its `async` default. Verified by resolving the effective\nconfig against both table names on the same file:\n\n    [tool.rebar.llm] overlap_drain = \"always\"  ->  effective 'async'   (NOT parsed)\n    [llm]            overlap_drain = \"always\"  ->  effective 'always'  (parsed)\n\nThe failure is silent in a second way: `_llm_drain_mode` (`src/rebar/llm/config.py:447`) maps any\nunrecognized value back to the default, so a typo also reads as \"enrichment is off\" while it is on.\n\n**2. The shipped default floods the shared branch.** With `suggest_duplicate_tickets = true`\n(`rebar.toml:39`) and `overlap_drain` unset, every ticket write path spawns an opportunistic drain\n(`src/rebar/llm/enrich_drain.py:505` `maybe_drain`). Each enrichment cycle appends and separately\npushes `ENQUEUE_ENRICH` -> `CLAIM_ENRICH` -> `TICKET_DIGEST` -> `DONE_ENRICH`, so ~4 pushed commits\nper ticket. Measured on `origin/tickets`: ~1000-1400 commits/hour sustained since 2026-08-27\n21:00 UTC, against a prior baseline of ~20-90/hour.\n\nThat write rate starves every other writer. A fetch->merge->push recovery cycle costs 2.4-4.2s\nwhile competing pushes land every 2-4s, so a writer that falls behind never regains the lead. The\nobserved consequence was stores diverging without bound (one clone reached 619 unpushed commits)\nand cross-environment reads disagreeing — a signed ticket read as `unsigned` through the MCP\nserver while the local store showed a valid `completion-verifier` attestation.\n\n## Scope\n\nSet `overlap_drain = \"off\"` in the committed `[llm]` table, and correct the comment that names the\nwrong table. This is the project's own documented scoping knob, not a new mechanism:\n`suggest_duplicate_tickets` stays `true`, so plan-review keeps its advisory overlap suggestions;\nonly the opportunistic drain on ordinary write paths stops. `maybe_drain` returns at\n`enrich_drain.py:525` before spawning anything.\n\nExplicitly OUT of scope: the retry/backoff defects and the store's failure to converge\n(`cibophobic-moist-guineafowl`, `b928-3ab6-5985-417b`). This ticket reduces the write pressure\nthat exposed them; it does not fix them.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `rebar.toml`'s `[llm]` table sets `overlap_drain = \"off\"`, and resolving the effective\n      config against the repo root returns `'off'` (checked by running the config resolver, not\n      by grepping the file — an invalid value silently falls back to the default).\n- [ ] The comment at `rebar.toml:38` names `[llm]`, the table that is actually parsed, so an\n      operator following it gets the effect it describes.\n- [ ] A regression test pins that `overlap_drain` is read from the `[llm]` table and that an\n      unparsed table name does NOT silently yield the default — the specific trap here is that\n      \"wrong table\" and \"correct table set to the default\" are indistinguishable from the\n      resolved value alone, so the test must use a non-default value to discriminate.\n- [ ] `suggest_duplicate_tickets` remains `true` and plan-review's advisory overlap path is\n      unchanged (checked: the existing overlap tests still pass).\n\n## Evidence\n\nEffective config on the three deployed writer containers was `async` before the change and `off`\nafter, read via the resolver inside each container rather than from file text.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"rebar.toml","reason":"set overlap_drain = \"off\" in the [llm] table (the parsed one) and correct the comment that names the never-parsed [tool.rebar.llm]"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_enrich_drain.py","reason":"regression test pinning that overlap_drain is read from the [llm] TOML table and that an unparsed table name does not silently yield the default; uses a non-default value to discriminate"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","b928-3ab6-5985-417b"],["relates_to","cde0-da07-78a4-4c23"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"3276463b-b0fa-4c8b-8a11-07727e20e591","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["tracker","config","docs","contention"],"ticket_id":"62ab-c11e-30c2-40be","ticket_type":"bug","title":"rebar.toml documents a never-parsed table for overlap_drain, and the drain default floods the shared tickets branch","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["51d7149c-abd2-4a6e-8bd5-997cf37ef60c","c83f95c1-4829-442d-812d-52849fd80c95","fe11ec65-c918-4d00-be85-5d71143cd393","3276463b-b0fa-4c8b-8a11-07727e20e591","8010d91f-055a-445f-97e9-05907653377c","a10cff3a-16c2-46d2-9f9c-a841f65ec51a","9936e5d1-c3b7-423e-99eb-5d6cbc1310bc"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787899599142983410,"uuid":"edfc9f38-f785-4426-8074-1c7b629cae1e"}